{"content":[{"c":["MARAH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Spring of water in the wilderness of Etham, the first camping place of the Israelites after crossing the Red Sea (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.15.23","r":"Exod.15.23","rawR":"Exod.15.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.15.23","value":"Exod.15.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 15:23"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Num.33.8-9","r":"Num.33.8-9","rawR":"Num.33.8-9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.33.8-9","value":"Num.33.8-9"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 33:8-9"},"). The accepted identification is with ‘Ain Hawarah, a pool of bitter water on the eastern coastal plain of the Gulf of Suez, about 44 miles (70.8 kilometers) southeast of Suez, and about 5 miles (8 kilometers) northwest of ‘Ain Gharandel, south of Wadi Amarah (which may preserve an echo of the ancient name)."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=WildernessWanderings_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"WildernessWanderings_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"WildernessWanderings_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Wilderness Wanderings"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Marah","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Ex 15:23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Exod.15.23","rawQueryValue":"Exod.15.23","sourceRefExact":"Exod.15.23"},{"anchorText":"Nm 33:8-9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.33.8-9","rawQueryValue":"Num.33.8-9","sourceRefExact":"Num.33.8-9"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"fc752322cc2707fcf55069c01085bdc71bd79a2d86da685cce720f1898111319","sourceItemName":"Marah","sourceItemOrder":129,"sourceMember":"Articles/M.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Marah","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","type